    "axis": "accessibility",
    "evidence": "Keyboard traversal and visible focus passed for all expected controls; no touch-target violations or section overflow were measured, and reduced-motion sampling found no changed elements. However, WCAG contrast remains unproven: axe returned serious incomplete contrast checks for nine chart labels at every viewport, plus header contrast incompletes on tablet/mobile. The charts’ accessible names are also compressed strings such as “100%0%25%50%75%100%,” which provide weak screen-reader context.",
